@startuml sequence
!include style.puml
title A day's steps, from the watch's sensors to Apple Health

box "Pixel Watch 4" #F6FDF8
  participant "Health\nServices" as HS #F2F2F7
  participant "DayLog" as DAY #EAF8EF
  participant "BridgeService" as SVC #EAF8EF
end box

box "iPhone" #F6FAFF
  participant "BridgeCentral" as BC #EAF2FC
  participant "HealthStore" as HS2 #EAF2FC
  participant "HealthKitSink" as SINK #EAF2FC
  participant "Apple Health" as HK #F2F2F7
end box

== Link ==

SVC -> SVC : advertise\n30s burst / 5min rest
BC -[#0A6ED1]> SVC : connect (bond keys)
note right of BC
  Encrypted + MITM-protected,
  or the watch refuses everything.
end note
BC -> SVC : discover services
BC -> SVC : subscribe (CCCD write)
SVC -> SVC : advertising off
BC -> SVC : {"t":"sync"}
BC -> SVC : {"t":"goal","steps":N}

== Steady state ==

HS -> DAY : STEPS_DAILY (absolute)
DAY -> DAY : raise only; re-anchor\nhardware counter
SVC -[#1DA34A]> BC : {"t":"day","steps":N,...}
SVC -[#B23A34]> BC : {"t":"hr","bpm":N} every 5s

== Mirror ==

BC -> HS2 : day record
HS2 -> SINK : sum our own samples\nfor the watch's date

alt store readable
  SINK --> HS2 : have = M
  note right of SINK
    An empty day is reported as
    errorNoData. That is zero,
    not a failure — treating it as
    one meant the first sample of
    a new day was never written.
  end note
  alt N > M
    HS2 -> SINK : write N − M
    SINK -[#1DA34A]> HK : step sample
  else N < M
    HS2 -> SINK : delete our samples, write N
    SINK -[#1DA34A]> HK : day replaced
  end
else phone locked / not authorised
  SINK --> HS2 : errorDatabaseInaccessible
  HS2 -> HS2 : keep the day queued
  note right of HS2
    Never dropped. Retried on the next
    push, on unlock, on an authorisation
    change, and on foreground.
  end note
end

== When it goes quiet ==

BC -> BC : no `day` for 20 min
BC -> SVC : {"t":"sync"} (probe)
BC -> BC : still nothing at 25 min
BC -> SVC : drop connection
note right of BC
  Reconnecting forces a fresh discovery
  and CCCD write — the part the watch
  is waiting for.
end note
@enduml
